IMPORT prelude

-- Business Names Registration Act 2011 (Commonwealth) -- must I register a business name, can I get the one I want, how
-- long does it last, and what happens if I trade under a name that is not registered to me?
--
-- SEAT: the business owner -- the entity carrying on a business under a name: the sole trader, the partners, the company
-- (Daniel's Jarrah Legal Technologies Pty Ltd). Every decision is phrased as that owner asks it, from facts the owner could
-- state. Where the Act speaks to ASIC or the Minister (ss 24, 25, 33, 34, 49, 55), the encoding says what it means for the
-- owner: ASIC must register the name, may cancel it, must give the owner notice and time.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 3 ("carrying on a business", "business name"); s 4 (business, tied to ABN entitlement); s 18 (the
-- offence of carrying on a business under an unregistered name, and its exceptions); s 19 (business names information in
-- documents); ss 18-21 penalties; s 23(2)(a)(ii) (applying while an ABN application is pending); s 24(1) (when ASIC must
-- register the name); s 25 (availability), with ss 27(2), 28(2A) (Ministerial determinations) and s 31(3), (6) (consent of
-- the holder); s 29(2) (priority not lost while the ABN is pending); s 30 (fee unpaid for 10 business days); s 32
-- (disqualification); s 33(2)-(5) (1 or 3 years, alternative periods); s 34(2), (5) (treating 28 days' silence as
-- refusal); s 35 (notifying changes within 28 days); s 47 (cancellation for non-use); s 49(4), (5) (expiry and
-- cancellation); s 54(1)(b) (trading during the review period after cancellation); s 55(1), (8) (renewal).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 10, compilation date 1 July 2026 ("Includes amendments: Act No. 57, 2026"; register id
-- C2026C00334), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2011A00126.txt (retrieved 2026-10-13).
-- Also used: Crimes Act 1914, Compilation No. 167, compilation date 27 August 2026 (register id C2026C00368), as deposited
-- at ../../../crimes-act-1914/registers/source-bundle/C1914A00012.txt: s 4AA (penalty unit) and s 4B(3) (bodies corporate,
-- five times) only. s 4AA(3) indexes the $330 penalty unit from 1 July 2026 by a formula whose result is not in the
-- deposit, so the dollar value of a penalty unit is an INPUT. The Minister's instruments under ss 26, 27(1) and 28(1)
-- (identical names, undesirable names, restricted words), the Business Names Registration (Fees) Act 2011 and its fee
-- amounts, and any regulations under s 18(2)(h) are not deposited; what they decide is asked as a fact.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the s 20 duty to display the name (only its penalty); s 21's offence beyond its penalty; the application's
-- form and contents beyond the ABN (s 23); priority between competing applications beyond s 29(2); ASIC's other
-- cancellation grounds (ss 42-46, 48, 50, 51) and the notice periods in them; the register and access to it (ss 22,
-- 60-62); review (Part 7); partnerships, associations, trusts and joint ventures (Part 10) beyond the s 18(2)(c) own-name
-- exception; the Transitional Act; machinery (ss 1, 2, 6-15, 63-80, 90). Borrowed terms asked as facts: ABN entitlement
-- (see the ABN Act baseline beside this one), corporation, government body, notified State/Territory register,
-- "identical or nearly identical", "undesirable", restricted word, director disqualification under Corporations Act s 206B.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the design defaults ruled on
-- 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use as advice.
-- Judgments the Act hands to ASIC or the Minister are INPUTS ("if ASIC is satisfied that ...").

§ `Business Names Registration Act 2011`

§§ `ss 3, 4 -- is what I do a business`

-- s 4(1): "Business means an activity, or series of activities, done: (a) in the form of a profession, a trade,
-- employment, a vocation or a calling; or (b) in the form of an adventure or concern in the nature of trade; or (c) on a
-- regular or continuous basis, in the form of a lease, licence or other grant of an interest in property."
-- (2): "Business does not include an activity, or a series of activities, done in circumstances in which an entity doing
-- that activity or series of activities in, or in connection with, Australia would not be entitled to an ABN."
-- Plain gloss: a business is trading, a one-off venture or regular letting -- but only if it would earn you an ABN.
DECLARE `Form of my activity` IS ONE OF
    `a profession, trade, employment, vocation or calling`
    `an adventure or concern in the nature of trade`
    `a regular or continuous lease, licence or other grant of an interest in property`
    `none of these`

-- s 3: "carrying on a business includes doing anything in the course of the commencement or termination of the
-- business." "business name means a name used, or to be used, in relation to one or more businesses."
-- s 5: an entity is an individual, body corporate, partnership, other unincorporated body, trust or superannuation fund.
-- s 18(2)(a)-(c), (f) turn on the kind of entity; corporation and government body are borrowed and asked.
DECLARE `Kind of entity` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a corporation`
    `a partnership`
    `a government body`
    `another entity, such as a trust or an unincorporated association`

DECLARE `Me and the name` HAS
    `I am` IS A `Kind of entity`
    @desc What kind of entity you are (s 5)
    `my activity's form` IS A `Form of my activity`
    @desc Which form in s 4(1) your activity takes, if any
    `I would be entitled to an ABN for it` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether, doing this activity in or in connection with Australia, you would be entitled to an ABN (ABN Act s 8; see the ABN Act baseline)
    `I am carrying it on, starting it up or winding it up` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether you are carrying on the activity, or doing anything in the course of starting it or ending it
    `I carry it on under the name` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether you carry it on (or are setting it up) under the name in question
    `the name is registered to me on the Business Names Register` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the name is registered to you, as this entity, on ASIC's Business Names Register
    `the name is exactly my own name` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc For an individual: your own name; for a corporation: its own name; for a partnership: a name made up of all the partners' names
    `the name is registered to me on a notified State or Territory register` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the name is registered to you on a notified State/Territory register (s 6)
    `a law names me by it` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether a Commonwealth, State or Territory Act or instrument specifies the name as your name
    `I am a notified successor for the name` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether you are entered on the Register as a notified successor for the name (deceased estates, s 40(4))
    `a prescribed exception applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether a circumstance prescribed by regulations under s 18(2)(h) applies (the regulations are not deposited)
    `I notified ASIC of the holder's consent within the last 3 months` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the name's holder consented to registration to you, and you notified ASIC of that consent less than 3 months ago (s 31(4)-(6))
    `my registration was cancelled and its review period is running` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether ASIC cancelled your registration of the name and you are within the review period (4 months from notice, or longer if ASIC set one) (s 54)

@export Is what I do a business under the Business Names Registration Act (s 4)?
GIVEN `me` IS A `Me and the name` @desc Who you are and what you do
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I do a business` IF
        (NOT (`me`'s `my activity's form` EQUALS `none of these`))
    AND `me`'s `I would be entitled to an ABN for it`

@export Am I carrying on a business under the name (s 3)?
GIVEN `me` IS A `Me and the name` @desc Who you are and what you do
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I carrying on a business under the name` IF
        `Is what I do a business` `me`
    AND `me`'s `I am carrying it on, starting it up or winding it up`
    AND `me`'s `I carry it on under the name`

§§ `s 18 -- must I register the name`

-- s 18(1): "An entity commits an offence if: (a) the entity carries on a business under a name; and (b) the name is not
-- registered to the entity as a business name on the Business Names Register. Penalty: 30 penalty units."
-- (2): "Subsection (1) does not apply if: (a) the entity is an individual and the name is the individual's name; or (b) the
-- entity is a corporation and the name is the corporation's name; or (c) the entity is a partnership and the name consists
-- of all of the partners' names; or (d) the name is registered to the entity on a notified State/Territory register; or
-- (e) an Act ... specifies the name as the name of the entity; or (f) the entity is a government body; or (g) the entity
-- is a notified successor in relation to the name; or (h) other circumstances prescribed by the regulations ... apply."
-- (3): "Subsection (1) is an offence of strict liability."
-- s 31(6): a potential applicant who has notified ASIC of the holder's consent "does not commit an offence under subsection
-- 18(1) if the potential applicant carries on a business under the business name during the period of 3 months".
-- s 54(1)(b): after a cancellation, "the entity does not commit an offence under subsection 18(1) if the entity carries on
-- a business under the business name during the review period".
-- The own-name exception exists only for individuals, corporations and partnerships: a trust or an association has none.
DECLARE `Do I need to register the name` IS ONE OF
    `no: what I do is not a business under s 4`
    `no: I am not carrying on a business under the name`
    `no: the name is registered to me`
    `no: it is my own name`
    `no: it is registered to me on a notified State or Territory register`
    `no: a law names me by it`
    `no: I am a government body`
    `no: I am a notified successor for the name`
    `no: a prescribed exception applies`
    `not yet: I may trade under it for 3 months after notifying ASIC of the holder's consent`
    `not yet: I may trade under it during the review period after cancellation`
    `yes: I must register it, or I commit the s 18(1) offence`

GIVEN `me` IS A `Me and the name`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the own-name exception mine` IF
        `me`'s `the name is exactly my own name`
    AND (CONSIDER `me`'s `I am`
         WHEN `an individual` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a corporation` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a partnership` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

@export Must I register this business name, and if not, why not (s 18)?
GIVEN `me` IS A `Me and the name` @desc Who you are, what you do and the name you use
GIVETH A `Do I need to register the name`
DECIDE `Must I register the business name` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `Is what I do a business` `me`) THEN `no: what I do is not a business under s 4`
        IF (NOT `Am I carrying on a business under the name` `me`) THEN `no: I am not carrying on a business under the name`
        IF `me`'s `the name is registered to me on the Business Names Register` THEN `no: the name is registered to me`
        IF `Is the own-name exception mine` `me` THEN `no: it is my own name`
        IF `me`'s `the name is registered to me on a notified State or Territory register`
            THEN `no: it is registered to me on a notified State or Territory register`
        IF `me`'s `a law names me by it` THEN `no: a law names me by it`
        IF `me`'s `I am` EQUALS `a government body` THEN `no: I am a government body`
        IF `me`'s `I am a notified successor for the name` THEN `no: I am a notified successor for the name`
        IF `me`'s `a prescribed exception applies` THEN `no: a prescribed exception applies`
        IF `me`'s `I notified ASIC of the holder's consent within the last 3 months`
            THEN `not yet: I may trade under it for 3 months after notifying ASIC of the holder's consent`
        IF `me`'s `my registration was cancelled and its review period is running`
            THEN `not yet: I may trade under it during the review period after cancellation`
        OTHERWISE `yes: I must register it, or I commit the s 18(1) offence`

@export Do I commit the offence of carrying on a business under an unregistered business name (s 18(1))?
GIVEN `me` IS A `Me and the name` @desc Who you are, what you do and the name you use
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I commit the unregistered business name offence` IF
    `Must I register the business name` `me` EQUALS `yes: I must register it, or I commit the s 18(1) offence`

§§ `ss 18-21 and Crimes Act ss 4AA, 4B(3) -- what can I be fined`

-- s 18(1) and s 21(1): "Penalty: 30 penalty units." s 19(1) and s 20(1): "Penalty: 5 penalty units."
-- Crimes Act s 4B(3): a body corporate may be fined "not exceeding an amount equal to 5 times the amount of the maximum
-- pecuniary penalty that could be imposed by the court on a natural person convicted of the same offence."
-- Crimes Act s 4AA(1): "penalty unit means the amount of $330 (subject to indexation under subsection (3))."
DECLARE `Business names offence` IS ONE OF
    `trading under an unregistered business name (s 18)`
    `leaving the business name off a business document (s 19)`
    `not displaying the business name where the business is open to the public (s 20)`
    `trading under a business name while disqualified (s 21)`

@export What is the most I can be fined for this offence, in penalty units (ss 18-21; Crimes Act s 4B(3))?
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Business names offence` @desc Which offence
      `I am a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a body corporate, such as a company
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Most penalty units for the offence` IS
    `units for a natural person` TIMES (IF `I am a body corporate` THEN 5 ELSE 1)
    WHERE
        `units for a natural person` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the offence`
            WHEN `trading under an unregistered business name (s 18)` THEN 30
            WHEN `trading under a business name while disqualified (s 21)` THEN 30
            OTHERWISE 5

@export What is the most I can be fined for this offence, in dollars, at a given penalty unit value?
GIVEN `the offence` IS A `Business names offence` @desc Which offence
      `I am a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a body corporate, such as a company
      `dollars per penalty unit` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of a Commonwealth penalty unit on the day of the offence (Crimes Act s 4AA; $330 before indexation on 1 July 2026)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Most dollars for the offence` IS
    `Most penalty units for the offence` `the offence` `I am a body corporate` TIMES `dollars per penalty unit`

§§ `s 19 -- what my business documents must show`

-- s 19(2): "Business names information means the name and, if the entity has an ABN, the entity's ABN, where the business
-- document is of one of the following kinds: (a) a document that is lodged with ASIC; (b) a statement of account
-- (including an invoice); (c) a receipt; (d) an order for goods or services; (e) a cheque; (f) a promissory note or bill
-- of exchange; (g) an offer to provide goods or services (rather than an invitation to treat)." (3): "In any other case,
-- business names information means the name."
-- (4) repeats the s 18(2) exceptions and adds a Ministerial exemption; they are asked as one fact here.
DECLARE `Kind of business document` IS ONE OF
    `a document lodged with ASIC`
    `an invoice or other statement of account`
    `a receipt`
    `an order for goods or services`
    `a cheque, promissory note or bill of exchange`
    `an offer to provide goods or services`
    `another business document, such as a letter or an advertisement`

DECLARE `What my document must show` IS ONE OF
    `the business name and my ABN`
    `the business name`
    `nothing under s 19: an exception in s 19(4) applies`

@export What must my business document show (s 19)?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `Kind of business document` @desc What kind of written business communication it is
      `I have an ABN` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have an ABN
      `an exception in s 19(4) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether one of the s 19(4) exceptions applies (your own name, a government body, a Ministerial exemption, and the others)
GIVETH A `What my document must show`
DECIDE `What must my business document show` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `an exception in s 19(4) applies` THEN `nothing under s 19: an exception in s 19(4) applies`
        IF `I have an ABN` AND (NOT (`the document` EQUALS `another business document, such as a letter or an advertisement`))
            THEN `the business name and my ABN`
        OTHERWISE `the business name`

§§ `s 25 -- is the name available to me`

-- s 25: "A business name is available to an entity if: (a) the name is not identical or nearly identical to: (i) a
-- business name registered to another entity; or (ii) a name that is reserved or registered under the Corporations Act
-- 2001 for another body; or (iii) a name that is registered to another entity on a notified State/Territory register; or
-- (iv)-(vii) [names of government bodies and names given by statute, notified to ASIC]; and (b) a name that is identical or
-- nearly identical is not held under section 54 ...; and (c) no other entity has priority over a name that is identical or
-- nearly identical; and (d) either: (i) the name is not of a kind that is undesirable; or (ii) ... the Minister has
-- determined under subsection 27(2) that the name is available to the entity; and (e) any of the following applies: (i)
-- the name is not constituted by, and does not include, a restricted word or expression; (ii) ... restricted unless a
-- condition is satisfied, and the entity satisfies the condition; (iii) ... the Minister has determined under subsection
-- 28(2A) that the name is available to the entity."
-- s 31(3): if the holder lodges a consent notice and asks ASIC to cancel its registration, "the business name is taken to
-- be available to the applicant."
-- "Identical or nearly identical" (Minister's rules, s 26), "undesirable" (s 27(1)) and "restricted" (s 28(1)) are set
-- by instruments not deposited; they are asked as facts.
DECLARE `The name I want` HAS
    `it is identical or nearly identical to a name already taken by someone else` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether it is identical or nearly identical to a business name registered to another entity, a company name reserved or registered for another body, a name on a notified State/Territory register, or a notified government or statutory name (s 25(a))
    `an identical or nearly identical name is held during a review period` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether an identical or nearly identical name is held after a cancellation while its review period runs (s 54)
    `another applicant has priority over an identical or nearly identical name` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether another entity applied earlier for an identical or nearly identical name (s 29)
    `it is of an undesirable kind` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether it is of a kind the Minister has determined undesirable (for example offensive) (s 27(1))
    `the Minister has made it available to me despite being undesirable` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the Minister has determined in writing that it is available to you (s 27(2))
    `it includes a restricted word or expression` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether it is or includes a restricted word or expression (s 28(1), (2))
    `the restriction is conditional and I satisfy the condition` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the word is restricted only unless a condition is met, and you meet it
    `the Minister has made it available to me despite the restricted word` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the Minister has determined in writing that it is available to you (s 28(2A))
    `the holder has consented and asked ASIC to cancel its registration` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the entity the name is registered to has lodged both a consent to registration to you and a request to cancel its own (s 31(3))

DECLARE `Is the name available` IS ONE OF
    `available: the holder has consented and asked to cancel its registration`
    `not available: it is identical or nearly identical to a name already taken`
    `not available: an identical or nearly identical name is held during a review period`
    `not available: another applicant has priority`
    `not available: it is undesirable`
    `not available: it includes a restricted word`
    `available`

@export Is the business name I want available to me, and if not, why not (ss 25, 31(3))?
GIVEN `the name` IS A `The name I want` @desc The facts about the name you want
GIVETH A `Is the name available`
DECIDE `Is the business name available to me` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the name`'s `the holder has consented and asked ASIC to cancel its registration`
            THEN `available: the holder has consented and asked to cancel its registration`
        IF `the name`'s `it is identical or nearly identical to a name already taken by someone else`
            THEN `not available: it is identical or nearly identical to a name already taken`
        IF `the name`'s `an identical or nearly identical name is held during a review period`
            THEN `not available: an identical or nearly identical name is held during a review period`
        IF `the name`'s `another applicant has priority over an identical or nearly identical name`
            THEN `not available: another applicant has priority`
        IF `the name`'s `it is of an undesirable kind` AND (NOT `the name`'s `the Minister has made it available to me despite being undesirable`)
            THEN `not available: it is undesirable`
        IF     `the name`'s `it includes a restricted word or expression`
           AND (NOT `the name`'s `the restriction is conditional and I satisfy the condition`)
           AND (NOT `the name`'s `the Minister has made it available to me despite the restricted word`)
            THEN `not available: it includes a restricted word`
        OTHERWISE `available`

GIVEN `the name` IS A `The name I want`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `The name is available` IF
        `Is the business name available to me` `the name` EQUALS `available`
    OR  `Is the business name available to me` `the name` EQUALS `available: the holder has consented and asked to cancel its registration`

§§ `s 32 -- am I disqualified`

-- s 32(1): "An entity is disqualified if: (a) the entity is a person disqualified from managing corporations under
-- subsection 206B(1) of the Corporations Act 2001 because the person is convicted of an offence; or (b) a person involved
-- in the management of the entity is [so] disqualified ...; or (c) the entity is a person who is not [so] disqualified ...,
-- but is convicted of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, a State, a Territory or a foreign country that involves
-- dishonesty and is punishable by imprisonment for at least 3 months; or (d) ... convicted of an offence against the law of
-- a foreign country that is punishable by imprisonment for a period of more than 12 months; or (e) a person involved in the
-- management of the entity ... is convicted of an offence referred to in paragraph (c) or (d)."
-- (2)(c), (d): for (c)-(e), "for a period of 5 years after the day on which [the person] is convicted" or, if imprisoned,
-- "5 years after the day on which [the person] is released from prison". (3): the Minister may determine that the entity
-- "is not disqualified despite the conviction".
-- One record per person: you, or a person involved in your management (for a company, its directors and managers).
DECLARE `A person's record` HAS
    `is currently disqualified from managing corporations under s 206B(1) for a conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the person is, right now, within a disqualification from managing corporations under Corporations Act s 206B(1) because of a conviction
    `has a conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the person has been convicted of an offence (Australian or foreign)
    `the offence involves dishonesty` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the offence involves dishonesty
    `the offence is against foreign law` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the offence is against the law of a foreign country
    `months of imprisonment the offence is punishable by` IS A NUMBER
    @desc The maximum term of imprisonment for the offence, in months
    `years since conviction or, if imprisoned, release` IS A NUMBER
    @desc Years since the conviction or, if the person served a term of imprisonment, since release from prison
    `the Minister has determined the conviction does not disqualify` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the Minister has determined under s 32(3) that the entity is not disqualified despite the conviction

@export Does this person's record make me disqualified from holding a business name (s 32)?
GIVEN `the person` IS A `A person's record` @desc The record of you, or of a person involved in your management
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does this record disqualify me` IF
        (NOT `the person`'s `the Minister has determined the conviction does not disqualify`)
    AND (    `the person`'s `is currently disqualified from managing corporations under s 206B(1) for a conviction`
         OR  (    `the person`'s `has a conviction`
              AND `the person`'s `years since conviction or, if imprisoned, release` < 5
              AND (    (    `the person`'s `the offence involves dishonesty`
                        AND `the person`'s `months of imprisonment the offence is punishable by` >= 3)
                   OR  (    `the person`'s `the offence is against foreign law`
                        AND `the person`'s `months of imprisonment the offence is punishable by` > 12))))

§§ `ss 23, 24, 29(2) -- must ASIC register the name to me`

-- s 23(2)(a)(ii): the application must include "the entity's ABN or, if an application for an ABN is pending, a statement
-- to that effect and the reference number for the ABN application".
-- s 24(1): "ASIC must register the business name to the entity if ASIC is satisfied that: (a) the entity has an ABN; and
-- (b) the registration fee has been paid; and (c) the name is available to the entity; and (d) the entity is not
-- disqualified."
-- s 29(2): "the priority of an entity over a business name is not affected by the fact that an ABN application by the
-- entity is pending."
-- s 24 says only when ASIC must register; so the other outcomes are "ASIC need not register it" (ASIC may refuse, s 34).
-- The outcome holds as ASIC is satisfied of these facts.
DECLARE `What happens to my business name application` IS ONE OF
    `ASIC must register the name to me`
    `ASIC need not register it yet: I have no ABN (I may apply while my ABN application is pending)`
    `ASIC need not register it: the registration fee is not paid`
    `ASIC need not register it: the name is not available to me`
    `ASIC need not register it: I am disqualified`

@export Must ASIC register the business name to me (s 24)?
GIVEN `I have an ABN` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether ASIC is satisfied you have an ABN
      `I have paid the registration fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether ASIC is satisfied the registration fee has been paid
      `the name` IS A `The name I want` @desc The facts about the name you want
      `I am disqualified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are disqualified (s 32)
GIVETH A `What happens to my business name application`
DECIDE `What happens to my application for the name` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `I have an ABN`)
            THEN `ASIC need not register it yet: I have no ABN (I may apply while my ABN application is pending)`
        IF (NOT `I have paid the registration fee`) THEN `ASIC need not register it: the registration fee is not paid`
        IF (NOT `The name is available` `the name`) THEN `ASIC need not register it: the name is not available to me`
        IF `I am disqualified` THEN `ASIC need not register it: I am disqualified`
        OTHERWISE `ASIC must register the name to me`

§§ `ss 30, 34 -- an unpaid fee, and a silent ASIC`

-- s 30(2): "The application is taken to have been refused if the registration fee is not paid before the end of the fee
-- payment period." (3): the period "begins at the time at which the application is lodged and ends immediately before that
-- time on the day 10 business days after the day on which the application is lodged."
-- Read: refused once 10 business days have run since lodging (an inference about the time of day).
@export Is my business name application taken to be refused because I have not paid the fee (s 30)?
GIVEN `I have paid the registration fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid the registration fee
      `business days since I lodged` IS A NUMBER @desc Business days since the day you lodged the application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my application refused for the unpaid fee` IF
    (NOT `I have paid the registration fee`) AND `business days since I lodged` >= 10

-- s 34(2): "If ASIC has not decided an application ... within 28 days after the application is lodged, the entity may, at
-- any time, lodge with ASIC notice that the entity wishes to treat the application as having been refused." (5): disregard
-- each period from ASIC's s 24(2) request for information to the day the entity gives it. (4)(b): the fee is then refunded.
-- As in the ABN Act baseline, the right arises once more than 28 counted days have passed (an inference).
@export May I treat my business name application as refused because ASIC has not decided it (s 34(2), (5))?
GIVEN `ASIC has decided it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether ASIC has decided your application
      `days since I lodged` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since your application was lodged
      `days spent waiting on information ASIC asked me for` IS A NUMBER @desc Total days from each ASIC request for information to the day you gave it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I treat my business name application as refused` IF
        (NOT `ASIC has decided it`)
    AND `days since I lodged` - `days spent waiting on information ASIC asked me for` > 28

§§ `s 33 -- how long does registration last`

-- s 33(2): "The registration period ... must be a period of either 1 year or 3 years, unless an alternative registration
-- period is determined by ASIC under subsection (3) or (4)." (3): for "a company" aligning expiry "with the company's
-- review date"; (4): aligning with "another business name ... registered to the entity". (5): "an alternative registration
-- period must be: (a) if the registration period would otherwise have been 1 year--of no more than 18 months; and (b) if
-- ... 3 years--of no more than 3 years and 6 months." s 55(7) sets the same limits on renewal.
DECLARE `Registration term` IS ONE OF
    `1 year`
    `3 years`

@export How many months does my business name registration last (s 33(2))?
GIVEN `the term I choose` IS A `Registration term` @desc The period you ask for: 1 year or 3 years
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Months of registration` IS
    CONSIDER `the term I choose`
    WHEN `1 year` THEN 12
    WHEN `3 years` THEN 36

@export May ASIC give me an alternative registration period (s 33(3), (4))?
GIVEN `I asked for one in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you lodged a request in the prescribed form and manner
      `I am a company and it aligns expiry with my review date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a company and the period would make the name expire on the company's review date
      `it aligns expiry with another business name of mine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether another business name is registered to you and the period would make both expire on the same day
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May ASIC give me an alternative registration period` IF
        `I asked for one in the prescribed form`
    AND (`I am a company and it aligns expiry with my review date` OR `it aligns expiry with another business name of mine`)

@export What is the longest alternative registration period I can be given, in months (ss 33(5), 55(7))?
GIVEN `the term it replaces` IS A `Registration term` @desc The 1-year or 3-year period that would otherwise apply
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Longest alternative registration period in months` IS
    CONSIDER `the term it replaces`
    WHEN `1 year` THEN 18
    WHEN `3 years` THEN 42

§§ `ss 49, 55 -- renewal and expiry`

-- s 55(1): "An entity may renew the registration ... for a period of 1 year or 3 years by lodging the renewal fee". (8):
-- renewal "no earlier than 2 months before the expiry of the registration period". (9): "The period of registration on
-- renewal begins immediately after the end of the immediately preceding registration period."
-- s 49(5): "a business name continues to be registered to an entity after the expiry of the registration period ...
-- unless the registration is cancelled." So renewal stays open after expiry until cancellation (an inference from (5) and
-- (8) together).
@export May I renew my business name registration now (s 55(8), s 49(5))?
GIVEN `months until expiry` IS A NUMBER @desc Months until your registration period ends (negative if it has already ended)
      `my registration has been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether ASIC has cancelled the registration
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I renew now` IF
    (NOT `my registration has been cancelled`) AND `months until expiry` <= 2

-- s 49(1): ASIC "must, at least 28 days before the registration period ... expires, remind the entity in writing". (3):
-- after expiry ASIC "may give notice in writing ... that ASIC will cancel the registration unless it is renewed". (4):
-- ASIC "may cancel ... with effect on the later of: (a) the end of a period of 3 months beginning when the registration
-- expires; and (b) the end of a period of 6 weeks beginning on the day on which notice is given in accordance with
-- subsection (3)." Read: without a s 49(3) notice there is no date under (b), so no cancellation (an inference).
@export Can ASIC cancel my expired business name yet (s 49(3), (4))?
GIVEN `months since expiry` IS A NUMBER @desc Months since the registration period ended
      `I have been given notice that it will be cancelled unless renewed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether ASIC has given you the s 49(3) notice
      `days since that notice` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since that notice was given
      `I have renewed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have renewed the registration
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can ASIC cancel my expired name yet` IF
        (NOT `I have renewed`)
    AND `months since expiry` >= 3
    AND `I have been given notice that it will be cancelled unless renewed`
    AND `days since that notice` >= 42

§§ `ss 35, 47 -- keeping the name`

-- s 35(1): if information the entity gave ASIC is recorded in the Register and "circumstances change so that the
-- information is no longer correct; the entity must lodge with ASIC notice of the change within 28 days after becoming
-- aware of it." (s 48 lets ASIC cancel for a failure, if satisfied it affects the integrity of the Register.)
@export Am I late telling ASIC about a change to my business name details (s 35)?
GIVEN `the recorded information is no longer correct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether information you gave ASIC, recorded against the business name, is no longer correct
      `days since I became aware of the change` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since you became aware of the change
      `I have lodged notice of the change` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have lodged notice of the change in the prescribed form
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I late telling ASIC about the change` IF
        `the recorded information is no longer correct`
    AND (NOT `I have lodged notice of the change`)
    AND `days since I became aware of the change` > 28

-- s 47(1): ASIC "may cancel the registration ... if: (a) ASIC is satisfied that: (i) the entity is not carrying on a
-- business under the business name; and (ii) the entity has not, in the immediately preceding period of 3 months, carried
-- on a business under the business name; and (b) the entity is not a government body; and (c) ASIC is not satisfied that
-- there are exceptional circumstances justifying the failure". (2): at least 28 days' notice, inviting evidence.
@export Can ASIC cancel my business name because I am not using it (s 47)?
GIVEN `I am trading under it now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are carrying on a business under the name now
      `I traded under it in the last 3 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you carried on a business under it in the immediately preceding 3 months
      `I am a government body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a government body
      `ASIC is satisfied there are exceptional circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether ASIC is satisfied exceptional circumstances justify the non-use
      `days of notice ASIC has given me` IS A NUMBER @desc Days since ASIC gave you written notice of its intention, inviting evidence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can ASIC cancel my name for non-use` IF
        (NOT `I am trading under it now`)
    AND (NOT `I traded under it in the last 3 months`)
    AND (NOT `I am a government body`)
    AND (NOT `ASIC is satisfied there are exceptional circumstances`)
    AND `days of notice ASIC has given me` >= 28
